# The collection's own tools -- what makes this a collection rather than a
# heap of binaries.
shot    keep
cap     keep is how a program leaves this disk for your own: it copies the
cap     binary AND whatever it needs.  Dry run first, which is what -n is
cap     for -- nothing is written here.
run     /dd/CMDS/keep -n hack
wait    6

shot    kept
cap     kept lists what has been taken and what it came to.
run     /dd/CMDS/kept
wait    5

shot    about-tar
for     about
cap     about answers for any program on the disk, out of the same four
cap     files the web catalogue is built from.
run     /dd/CMDS/about elvis
wait    5

shot    ask
cap     ask and ynad put a question to the person running a script and set
cap     the status from the answer.
run     /dd/CMDS/ask "Shall I go on"
wait    3
send    y
wait    3

shot    every
cap     every runs a command at intervals; repeat runs it over and over.
run     /dd/CMDS/repeat 3 /dd/CMDS/date
wait    8
